---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import InterestForm from "../components/InterestForm.astro";
import { listingsByCategory } from "../data/directory";
import { parishes } from "../data/parishes";

const agents = listingsByCategory("property");
---

<Base
  title="Properties in Andorra | How we list homes"
  description="How Andorra Private will list homes: parish, type and situation. No invented houses or borrowed photographs. AGIA-registered agents."
  path="/properties"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Properties</h1>
    <p>
      Homes for people who will live here, not a scraped portal. Until we
      have a file we have seen, the list stays empty.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose wide">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        We do not invent houses, prices or photographs. Nothing on this
        page is an offer. Buying or renting usually means an
        AGIA-registered agent, a notary, and for non-residents the
        current foreign-investment rules.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>How a listing will look</h2>
    <p>
      When a home is ready, it will use the same card as the rest of the
      site. The cards below are a template, not houses for sale.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="listing-card">
        <div class="listing-meta">Template · fields</div>
        <h3>Parish · type · status</h3>
        <p>
          Valley apartment, village house or high-valley chalet. No
          borrowed photograph. No guessed price.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="listing-card">
        <div class="listing-meta">Template · what we will state</div>
        <h3>Only what we can stand behind</h3>
        <p>
          Parish, approximate setting, bedrooms if confirmed, and whether
          it is for sale, to let, or a private introduction. Source named.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="listing-card">
        <div class="listing-meta">Template · not published</div>
        <h3>What we will not do</h3>
        <p>
          Stock mountain photographs, copied agency galleries, invented
          inventories, or “from €…” figures we have not been given in
          writing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="empty-listings">
      <div class="listing-meta">Current selection</div>
      <h3>No public listings yet</h3>
      <p>
        The structure is ready. When a property is cleared for this site
        it will appear here, parish by parish. Until then, leave an email
        or speak to a licensed agent.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Where people look</h2>
    <p>
      The seven parishes are not interchangeable. The capital and Escaldes
      are practical. Ordino and Canillo are higher. La Massana and Encamp
      sit on ski valleys. Sant Julià is the southern gate. Read the
      <a href="/where-to-live">where to live</a>
      before you instruct a search.
    </p>
    <div class="card-grid">
      {
        parishes.map((parish) => (
          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-label">{parish.label}</div>
            <h3>{parish.name}</h3>
            <p>{parish.summary}</p>
            <a href="/where-to-live" class="text-link">
              Parish note
            </a>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <h2>Licensed agents</h2>
    <p>
      The official college of estate agents is
      <a href="https://www.agia.ad/collegiats" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >AGIA</a
      >. We list a first set of member firms that publish their own sites.
      That is not an endorsement, and it is not the full register.
    </p>
    <div class="card-grid">
      {
        agents.map((agent) => (
          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-label">AGIA register</div>
            <h3>{agent.name}</h3>
            <p>{agent.summary}</p>
            <a href={`/directory/${agent.slug}`} class="text-link">
              Directory note
            </a>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <p>
      Residence files often need proof of accommodation. If you are
      moving for a permit, read
      <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>
      first, then look at housing. Non-resident buyers should also read
      <a href="/buying-property">buying property</a>.
      Foreign-investment rules are not the same as a listing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <InterestForm
    intro="Leave an email if you are looking for a home in Andorra. We’ll write back."
    source="properties"
  />
</Base>
